The '''Allies of World War III''', were the countries that together opposed the [[Eurasian Coalition|Coalition forces]] during the [[World War III|Third World War]] (2051–2055). The Allies promoted the alliance as seeking to stop Turkish, and Japanese aggression.

The leaders of the "Big Four" – the United States, Poland, China, and Britain – controlled Allied strategy; relations between Britain and the United States were especially close.

